 * arbitrary size.
 *
 * <p>The text field will copy the currently selected text when ctrl+c is 
pressed, and paste any
 * text in the clipboard when ctrl+v is pressed. Clipboard functionality is 
provided via the {@link
 * Clipboard} interface. Currently there are two standard implementations, one 
for the desktop and
 * one for Android. The Android clipboard is a stub, as copy & pasting on 
Android is not supported
 * yet.
 *
 * <p>The text field allows you to specify an {@link OnscreenKeyboard} for 
displaying a softkeyboard
 * and piping all key events generated by the keyboard to the text field. There 
